WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Advertise your product or brand here
contact www.OpenSubtitles.org today

2
00:01:36.728 --> 00:01:47.691
<font color="#ec14bd">Sync & corrections by honeybunny</font>
<font color="#ec14bd">www.addic7ed.com</font>

3
00:02:02.569 --> 00:02:05.871
<i>Are you sure about this?</i>

4
00:02:05.906 --> 00:02:08.574
No.

5
00:02:08.608 --> 00:02:10.643
It's dangerous.

6
00:02:12.279 --> 00:02:15.247
If we take Tywin's
castle from him.

7
00:02:15.282 --> 00:02:18.550
the lords of Westeros will
realize he's not invincible.

8
00:02:18.618 --> 00:02:20.052
Take his home.

9
00:02:20.153 --> 00:02:22.187
take his gold. take his power.

10
00:02:22.222 --> 00:02:24.323
Why are you telling me?

11
00:02:28.027 --> 00:02:29.861
You begged me not to send Theon

12
00:02:29.896 --> 00:02:33.799
to negotiate with his father
and I ignored your advice.

13
00:02:36.002 --> 00:02:38.137
Now Winterfell is burnt
to the ground.

14
00:02:38.171 --> 00:02:40.339
the North is overrun
with ironborn.

15
00:02:40.373 --> 00:02:42.441
and Bran and Rickon are gone.

16
00:02:44.944 --> 00:02:46.845
So Casterly Rock...

17
00:02:51.317 --> 00:02:53.151
I'm asking your advice.

18
00:02:59.192 --> 00:03:01.426
We have enough men?

19
00:03:05.131 --> 00:03:07.266
If Walder Frey cooperates.

20
00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:10.269
If Walder Frey cooperates.

21
00:03:15.141 --> 00:03:18.477
If reinforcements arrive
from King's Landing

22
00:03:18.511 --> 00:03:20.879
<i>before we take the castle...</i>

23
00:03:22.248 --> 00:03:26.084
we'll be caught between
Tywin's army and the sea.

24
00:03:30.355 --> 00:03:33.857
We'll lose the war and die
the way Father died.

25
00:03:33.891 --> 00:03:35.892
Or worse.

26
00:03:40.864 --> 00:03:44.734
Show them how it feels
to lose what they love.

27
00:04:15.031 --> 00:04:17.533
<i>My honored guests...</i>

28
00:04:19.102 --> 00:04:21.604
be welcome within my walls

29
00:04:21.638 --> 00:04:23.439
and at my table.

30
00:04:25.476 --> 00:04:28.144
<i>I extend to you my hospitality</i>

31
00:04:28.179 --> 00:04:32.015
and protection
in the light of the Seven.

32
00:04:32.049 --> 00:04:34.685
We thank you for your
hospitality. my lord.

33
00:04:38.656 --> 00:04:41.525
I have come to make
my apologies. my lord.

34
00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:43.427
and to beg your forgiveness.

35
00:04:43.461 --> 00:04:46.830
Don't beg my forgiveness.
Your Grace.

36
00:04:48.233 --> 00:04:51.368
It wasn't me you spurned.
It was my girls.

37
00:05:03.381 --> 00:05:06.550
<i>One of them was supposed</i>
<i>to be queen.</i>

38
00:05:06.584 --> 00:05:08.251
Now none of them are.

39
00:05:09.387 --> 00:05:12.822
This is Arwyen my daughter.

40
00:05:12.857 --> 00:05:17.460
<i>My daughter Walda.</i>
<i>my daughter Derwa.</i>

41
00:05:17.494 --> 00:05:20.062
<i>my daughter Waldra.</i>

42
00:05:24.567 --> 00:05:26.802
My eldest granddaughters

43
00:05:26.837 --> 00:05:30.138
<i>Ginia and Neila.</i>

44
00:05:31.775 --> 00:05:36.212
<i>Serra and Sarra.</i>
<i>granddaughters. twins.</i>

45
00:05:36.246 --> 00:05:37.813
You could have had either.

46
00:05:37.847 --> 00:05:41.117
<i>Could have had both</i>
<i>for all I care.</i>

47
00:05:41.151 --> 00:05:43.585
My granddaughter Marianne.

48
00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:46.488
<i>My granddaughter Freya.</i>

49
00:05:47.924 --> 00:05:50.325
My granddaughter...

50
00:05:50.359 --> 00:05:51.960
Wertha.

51
00:05:54.196 --> 00:05:57.264
<i>Waldra.</i>

52
00:05:57.332 --> 00:05:59.300
Waldina.

53
00:05:59.368 --> 00:06:02.136
- I'm Merry.
- Fine.

54
00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:05.940
And here's my youngest
daughter Shirei.

55
00:06:05.975 --> 00:06:08.911
<i>though she hasn't bled yet.</i>

56
00:06:08.945 --> 00:06:11.814
Clearly you don't have
the patience for all that.

57
00:06:13.183 --> 00:06:14.817
My ladies.

58
00:06:14.851 --> 00:06:18.354
All men should keep their
word. kings most of all.

59
00:06:19.956 --> 00:06:22.925
I was pledged to marry one
of you and I broke that vow.

60
00:06:22.959 --> 00:06:25.127
<i>The fault is not with you.</i>

61
00:06:25.195 --> 00:06:28.564
<i>Any man would be lucky</i>
<i>to have any one of you.</i>

62
00:06:28.598 --> 00:06:31.500
<i>I did what I did</i>
<i>not to slight you.</i>

63
00:06:31.534 --> 00:06:33.369
but because I loved another.

64
00:06:33.403 --> 00:06:35.304
<i>I know these words</i>
<i>cannot set right</i>

65
00:06:35.338 --> 00:06:37.372
<i>the wrong I have done</i>
<i>to you and your house.</i>

66
00:06:37.407 --> 00:06:40.709
I beg your forgiveness

67
00:06:40.743 --> 00:06:43.845
and pledge to do
all I can to make amends

68
00:06:43.913 --> 00:06:46.715
so the Freys of the Crossing
and the Starks of Winterfell

69
00:06:46.783 --> 00:06:48.683
may once again be friends.

70
00:06:56.025 --> 00:06:57.893
<i>Very good.</i>

71
00:07:00.163 --> 00:07:02.030
There she is.

72
00:07:02.065 --> 00:07:04.199
<i>Come closer.</i>

73
00:07:04.233 --> 00:07:06.200
Let me have a look at you.

74
00:07:12.741 --> 00:07:15.342
Still can't see you.

75
00:07:15.376 --> 00:07:17.511
Old eyes.

76
00:07:32.228 --> 00:07:34.396
Love.

77
00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:38.301
<i>That's what the Starks</i>
<i>of Winterfell call it. eh?</i>

78
00:07:40.404 --> 00:07:42.438
Very honorable.

79
00:07:42.472 --> 00:07:44.740
I call it a pretty face.

80
00:07:44.775 --> 00:07:47.844
Mmm. very pretty.

81
00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:52.048
Prettier than this lot.
that's for sure.

82
00:07:53.918 --> 00:07:55.652
Very shapely as well.

83
00:07:57.288 --> 00:08:00.357
<i>Oh. you try to hide her</i>
<i>under that dress.</i>

84
00:08:00.391 --> 00:08:02.359
If you wanted to hide her.

85
00:08:02.394 --> 00:08:04.762
you shouldn't have brought her
here in the first place.

86
00:08:10.769 --> 00:08:12.437
I can always see

87
00:08:12.471 --> 00:08:15.306
what's going on
beneath a dress.

88
00:08:15.341 --> 00:08:18.243
<i>Been at this a long time.</i>

89
00:08:19.511 --> 00:08:22.146
<i>I bet when you take</i>
<i>that dress off.</i>

90
00:08:22.181 --> 00:08:24.882
everything stays
right where it is.

91
00:08:24.916 --> 00:08:26.716
Doesn't drop an inch.

92
00:08:28.686 --> 00:08:32.254
Your king says he betrayed
me for love.

93
00:08:32.289 --> 00:08:35.024
I say he betrayed me
for firm tits

94
00:08:35.058 --> 00:08:37.660
and a tight fit.

95
00:08:37.694 --> 00:08:40.362
And I can respect that.

96
00:08:42.131 --> 00:08:45.400
When I was your age.
I'd have broken 50 oaths

97
00:08:45.434 --> 00:08:48.869
to get into that
without a second thought.

98
00:08:52.274 --> 00:08:55.676
Well. I've enough room
in the hall for you lot.

99
00:08:55.711 --> 00:08:57.778
We'll set up tents outside

100
00:08:57.813 --> 00:09:00.181
with food and ale
for the rest of your men.

101
00:09:00.215 --> 00:09:02.383
Thank you. my lord.

102
00:09:05.654 --> 00:09:07.222
Well. let's get ready.

103
00:09:07.256 --> 00:09:09.291
The wine will flow red

104
00:09:09.325 --> 00:09:12.795
<i>and the music will play loud</i>

105
00:09:12.829 --> 00:09:17.033
and we'll put
this mess behind us.

106
00:09:26.243 --> 00:09:27.743
Where?

107
00:09:27.778 --> 00:09:29.378
There.

108
00:09:36.486 --> 00:09:39.355
There.
It's a back gate.

109
00:09:39.389 --> 00:09:42.291
My men use it when they
visit Yunkai's bed slaves.

110
00:09:42.326 --> 00:09:44.027
Your men. but not you?

111
00:09:44.061 --> 00:09:45.695
<i>I have no
interest in slaves.</i>

112
00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:47.998
A man cannot make love
to property.

113
00:09:51.236 --> 00:09:52.903
This is where
we enter the city.

114
00:09:52.971 --> 00:09:54.405
Very few guards.
They know me.

115
00:09:54.439 --> 00:09:55.940
They let me inside...

116
00:09:55.974 --> 00:09:58.209
We're not gonna sneak
an army through a back gate.

117
00:09:58.244 --> 00:10:01.213
I kill the guards.
I take your two best men

118
00:10:01.247 --> 00:10:04.616
and lead them through the back
streets. which I know well.

119
00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:06.751
and open the front gates.

120
00:10:06.785 --> 00:10:08.386
Then comes the army.

121
00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:11.055
Once the walls are breached.
the city will fall in hours.

122
00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:13.993
Or perhaps you'll lead Grey
Worm and me to the slaughter.

123
00:10:14.027 --> 00:10:16.495
cutting the head off our army.

124
00:10:16.530 --> 00:10:19.265
<i>The masters of Yunkai</i>
<i>will pay you your fee</i>

125
00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:20.667
and you won't have
to split it three ways

126
00:10:20.701 --> 00:10:22.702
'cause you've already
slaughtered your partners.

127
00:10:22.737 --> 00:10:25.205
You have
a very suspicious mind.

128
00:10:25.239 --> 00:10:28.308
In my experience. only dishonest
people think this way.

129
00:10:30.845 --> 00:10:32.679
You command the Unsullied.

130
00:10:32.713 --> 00:10:35.082
<i>What do you think?</i>

131
00:10:35.116 --> 00:10:37.684
_

132
00:10:37.954 --> 00:10:40.659
_

133
00:10:43.535 --> 00:10:46.962
_

134
00:10:47.895 --> 00:10:49.062
You leave tonight.

135
00:10:49.096 --> 00:10:51.197
Very good.

136
00:10:51.231 --> 00:10:53.032
We'll prepare.

137
00:10:58.104 --> 00:10:59.738
Ser Jorah.

138
00:11:01.841 --> 00:11:03.442
You can use an extra sword.

139
00:11:03.476 --> 00:11:05.978
You're the Queensguard.
Ser Barristan.

140
00:11:06.012 --> 00:11:08.047
Your place is by the queen.

141
00:11:08.081 --> 00:11:10.516
If we are truly
her loyal servants.

142
00:11:10.550 --> 00:11:12.585
we'll do whatever
needs to be done

143
00:11:12.619 --> 00:11:16.756
no matter the cost.
no matter our pride.

144
00:11:19.827 --> 00:11:22.329
We're west of Castle Black.

145
00:11:22.363 --> 00:11:24.364
but the Nightfort's
closest to us.

146
00:11:24.431 --> 00:11:27.534
It was the first
castle on the Wall.

147
00:11:27.568 --> 00:11:30.970
The Watch abandoned it during
the reign of King Jaehaerys I.

148
00:11:31.005 --> 00:11:34.674
Too big.
Impossible to maintain.

149
00:11:34.708 --> 00:11:37.043
Other than Castle Black itself.

150
00:11:37.077 --> 00:11:39.545
the Nightfort's
the perfect castle for us.

151
00:11:39.580 --> 00:11:43.049
It's got a secret sally port.

152
00:11:43.117 --> 00:11:45.685
the Black Gate.
as old as the Wall itself.

153
00:11:45.719 --> 00:11:49.455
No one's used it
in centuries most likely.

154
00:11:49.489 --> 00:11:52.157
It leads through the Wall

155
00:11:52.192 --> 00:11:54.092
right down into the Nightfort.

156
00:11:54.127 --> 00:11:55.994
if one knows how to find it.

157
00:11:56.029 --> 00:11:58.930
which. it just
so happens. I do.

158
00:12:03.569 --> 00:12:06.270
How do you know all that?

159
00:12:06.338 --> 00:12:10.241
I read about it
in a very old book.

160
00:12:15.747 --> 00:12:17.314
You know all that

161
00:12:17.348 --> 00:12:20.283
from staring at marks on paper?

162
00:12:21.352 --> 00:12:23.353
Yes.

163
00:12:23.421 --> 00:12:26.156
You're like a wizard.

164
00:12:41.307 --> 00:12:43.342
Our father used to tell us

165
00:12:43.376 --> 00:12:47.747
that no wildling ever looked
upon the Wall and lived.

166
00:12:47.782 --> 00:12:50.283
Here we are.

167
00:12:50.351 --> 00:12:52.653
Alive.

168
00:13:08.903 --> 00:13:11.671
Remember what happens
to children who run.

169
00:13:11.705 --> 00:13:14.541
I'm your father
and I'll do the talking.

170
00:13:24.452 --> 00:13:26.787
The roads have gone
right to hell. haven't they?

171
00:13:26.821 --> 00:13:28.956
Cracked three spokes
this morning.

172
00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:30.992
- Need a hand?
- Need about eight hands.

173
00:13:31.026 --> 00:13:32.960
Oh!

174
00:13:32.994 --> 00:13:35.162
Got to get this
salt pork to the Twins

175
00:13:35.197 --> 00:13:37.798
in time for the wedding.

176
00:13:37.833 --> 00:13:40.334
Many thanks.

177
00:13:42.504 --> 00:13:44.071
Don't!

178
00:13:44.105 --> 00:13:45.406
Don't kill him.

179
00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:47.608
Dead rats don't squeak.

180
00:13:47.642 --> 00:13:49.310
You're so dangerous.
aren't you?

181
00:13:49.377 --> 00:13:51.378
Saying scary things
to little girls.

182
00:13:51.413 --> 00:13:54.181
Killing little boys
and old people.

183
00:13:54.248 --> 00:13:55.649
A real hard man you are.

184
00:13:55.683 --> 00:13:57.651
More than anyone you know.

185
00:13:57.685 --> 00:14:00.420
You're wrong.
I know a killer.

186
00:14:00.455 --> 00:14:03.090
- A real killer.
- That so?

187
00:14:03.124 --> 00:14:04.725
You'd be like a kitten to him.

188
00:14:04.759 --> 00:14:07.094
He'd kill you
with his little finger.

189
00:14:07.128 --> 00:14:09.229
That him?

190
00:14:10.598 --> 00:14:12.632
- No.
- Good.

191
00:14:13.901 --> 00:14:15.602
Don't kill him.

192
00:14:15.669 --> 00:14:17.904
Please.

193
00:14:17.938 --> 00:14:20.073
Please don't.

194
00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:24.777
You're very kind.

195
00:14:24.812 --> 00:14:26.779
Someday it'll get you killed.

196
00:14:44.131 --> 00:14:45.965
Where are we?

197
00:14:46.032 --> 00:14:48.200
The Gift. I think.

198
00:14:48.235 --> 00:14:49.869
Brandon the Builder
gave all this land

199
00:14:49.903 --> 00:14:51.971
<i>south of the Wall</i>
<i>to the Night's Watch</i>

200
00:14:52.006 --> 00:14:54.941
for their sustenance
and support.

201
00:14:54.976 --> 00:14:57.244
Maester Luwin taught me that.

202
00:14:59.047 --> 00:15:01.315
Doesn't seem to be supporting
anyone at the moment.

203
00:15:01.349 --> 00:15:05.052
It's good land
and there's no war up here.

204
00:15:05.086 --> 00:15:06.587
Why leave?

205
00:15:06.654 --> 00:15:08.322
Wildlings.

206
00:15:08.356 --> 00:15:10.090
Sorry.

207
00:15:10.124 --> 00:15:12.826
But they come over
the Wall and raid.

208
00:15:12.893 --> 00:15:14.694
steal. carry off women.

209
00:15:14.728 --> 00:15:16.929
Old Nan said they turn
your skull into a cup

210
00:15:16.964 --> 00:15:19.031
and make you drink
your own blood from it.

211
00:15:21.701 --> 00:15:23.402
That's what Old Nan said.

212
00:15:23.436 --> 00:15:25.104
There's a storm coming.

213
00:15:26.473 --> 00:15:28.774
I don't see any...

214
00:15:32.278 --> 00:15:33.979
It's as good a place
to shelter as any.

215
00:15:37.250 --> 00:15:39.585
We can drink some blood
while we wait.

216
00:15:39.652 --> 00:15:41.753
I don't need much.

217
00:15:53.567 --> 00:15:56.002
Only one old man
and eight good horses.

218
00:15:56.069 --> 00:15:59.138
What's one old man
doing with eight horses?

219
00:15:59.172 --> 00:16:01.039
He breeds them for the Watch.

220
00:16:01.074 --> 00:16:03.042
How's he keep folks
from stealing them?

221
00:16:03.076 --> 00:16:05.411
The Watch protects him.

222
00:16:05.446 --> 00:16:07.680
Not today they don't.

223
00:16:07.715 --> 00:16:10.384
He's selling horses.
he's got some gold in there.

224
00:16:10.418 --> 00:16:13.620
<i>- And proper steel.</i>
- Let's carve him up.

225
00:16:13.655 --> 00:16:15.022
We just take the horses and go.

226
00:16:15.056 --> 00:16:17.725
The old man's no threat.

227
00:16:18.761 --> 00:16:20.194
I keep telling you.

228
00:16:20.228 --> 00:16:22.363
He's an old man.

229
00:16:22.397 --> 00:16:24.865
A spear through the heart's
a better way to die

230
00:16:24.933 --> 00:16:27.373
than coughing up your last with
no one but your horses to hear.

231
00:16:28.904 --> 00:16:32.239
The Watch might send a few men
looking for a horse thief.

232
00:16:32.274 --> 00:16:35.142
They'll send a lot more
to hunt down murderers.

233
00:16:35.177 --> 00:16:37.011
I hope so.

234
00:16:37.045 --> 00:16:39.981
Killing crows
in their castle is tough.

235
00:16:40.016 --> 00:16:41.950
Killing them out here
in the open.

236
00:16:42.017 --> 00:16:43.685
that's what we do.

237
00:16:43.719 --> 00:16:45.453
Spread out.

238
00:16:45.521 --> 00:16:48.056
Surround the hut and move in.

239
00:17:30.833 --> 00:17:32.066
Ygritte!

240
00:17:34.136 --> 00:17:36.637
<i>Clear the barn!</i>

241
00:18:13.808 --> 00:18:17.210
No one's going to believe you're a
hog farmer if you eat them all.

242
00:18:17.278 --> 00:18:19.546
Best part of the animal.

243
00:18:24.253 --> 00:18:26.454
Don't worry.
They're still there.

244
00:18:27.690 --> 00:18:29.291
I know they're still there.

245
00:18:29.325 --> 00:18:31.059
You check every five minutes

246
00:18:31.127 --> 00:18:33.661
like you're afraid
they're gonna move.

247
00:18:33.696 --> 00:18:35.463
I'm not afraid.

248
00:18:35.498 --> 00:18:37.732
Of course you are.

249
00:18:37.767 --> 00:18:40.068
You're almost there

250
00:18:40.102 --> 00:18:42.704
and you're afraid
you won't make it.

251
00:18:42.772 --> 00:18:46.141
The closer you get.
the worse the fear gets.

252
00:18:46.175 --> 00:18:49.612
No point in trying to hide
behind that face.

253
00:18:49.646 --> 00:18:52.548
<i>I know fear when I see it.</i>

254
00:18:52.582 --> 00:18:54.450
Seen it a lot.

255
00:18:55.752 --> 00:18:58.287
I knew fear
when I saw it in you.

256
00:18:59.756 --> 00:19:02.559
You're afraid of fire.

257
00:19:02.627 --> 00:19:04.328
When Beric's sword
went up in flames.

258
00:19:04.362 --> 00:19:06.196
you looked like
a scared little girl.

259
00:19:09.835 --> 00:19:12.169
And I know why. too.

260
00:19:14.039 --> 00:19:16.474
<i>I heard what</i>
<i>your brother did to you.</i>

261
00:19:17.610 --> 00:19:18.910
Pressed your face to the fire

262
00:19:18.978 --> 00:19:21.546
like you're a nice
juicy mutton chop.

263
00:19:25.351 --> 00:19:27.519
That give you some ideas?

264
00:19:30.356 --> 00:19:33.025
Might do.

265
00:19:33.059 --> 00:19:35.394
Go ahead. then.

266
00:19:35.428 --> 00:19:37.796
You might get away.

267
00:19:37.831 --> 00:19:40.366
Might even make it
there on your own.

268
00:19:41.434 --> 00:19:43.669
They're just over the river.

269
00:19:43.703 --> 00:19:45.838
The closest you've
been to family

270
00:19:45.872 --> 00:19:48.907
since Ilyn Payne
snipped your daddy's neck.

271
00:19:52.345 --> 00:19:55.347
Someday I'm gonna put
a sword through your eye

272
00:19:55.381 --> 00:19:57.015
and out the back of your skull.

273
00:20:21.739 --> 00:20:25.174
How are we going
to get past the Wall?

274
00:20:25.209 --> 00:20:27.143
My uncle said
it's 700 feet high.

275
00:20:32.483 --> 00:20:34.050
How did you get past it?

276
00:20:38.088 --> 00:20:40.823
Got in a boat and rowed
past the Bay of Seals.

277
00:20:40.858 --> 00:20:44.059
It would take us two months
to get to the Bay of Seals.

278
00:20:44.093 --> 00:20:46.228
Some climb straight up the ice.

279
00:20:46.295 --> 00:20:49.564
Even Hodor's not strong enough to
climb the Wall with me on his back.

280
00:20:49.632 --> 00:20:52.801
Hodor.

281
00:20:52.835 --> 00:20:55.370
19 castles guard the Wall.

282
00:20:55.405 --> 00:20:58.774
- Only three are still manned.
- Hodor!

283
00:20:58.809 --> 00:21:01.043
One of those abandoned fortresses
will give us a way through.

284
00:21:01.077 --> 00:21:03.312
My uncle said the gates were
sealed with ice and stone

285
00:21:03.346 --> 00:21:04.780
when the castles were deserted.

286
00:21:04.814 --> 00:21:08.117
Well. we'll have
to open them up again.

287
00:21:09.720 --> 00:21:12.455
- Whoa. whoa. whoa!
<i>- There's a rider out there.</i>

288
00:21:13.758 --> 00:21:15.692
Just one?

289
00:21:15.726 --> 00:21:17.494
<i>- There's more.</i>
- Hodor!

290
00:21:18.863 --> 00:21:20.363
Shh. Shh.

291
00:21:20.398 --> 00:21:23.133
- It's just thunder. sweet giant.
- Hodor.

292
00:21:23.201 --> 00:21:25.535
I yield.

293
00:21:25.603 --> 00:21:27.237
- <i>I yield.</i>
- Wildlings.

294
00:21:32.344 --> 00:21:33.845
Where's Shaggydog and Summer?

295
00:21:33.879 --> 00:21:35.880
Hunting.

296
00:21:35.948 --> 00:21:37.916
Hodor!

297
00:21:37.950 --> 00:21:40.251
- Shh. quiet. Hodor.
- Hodor!

298
00:21:40.319 --> 00:21:42.286
Make him shut up.
If they hear us...

299
00:21:42.321 --> 00:21:44.489
- Hush. Hodor. No... no more Hodoring.
- Hodor!

300
00:21:44.523 --> 00:21:47.425
- Hodor!
- Hodor. calm down.

301
00:21:47.460 --> 00:21:48.793
- You need to keep quiet.
- They're gonna hear us.

302
00:21:48.828 --> 00:21:50.995
<i>Hodor. be quiet.</i>

303
00:21:52.598 --> 00:21:54.666
- Ah! Hodor!
- Hodor. calm down.

304
00:21:54.734 --> 00:21:57.702
- Hodor! Hodor!
- Hodor. be quiet!

305
00:22:19.958 --> 00:22:21.659
What did you do?

306
00:22:21.693 --> 00:22:24.428
Nothing.

307
00:22:24.462 --> 00:22:26.397
I don't know.

308
00:22:30.502 --> 00:22:32.103
What's that?

309
00:22:33.338 --> 00:22:35.607
That's a horse dying.

310
00:22:45.684 --> 00:22:48.252
<i>Bring them over here.</i>

311
00:22:48.286 --> 00:22:51.455
<i>That was the last of them.
The rest are dead.</i>

312
00:22:51.489 --> 00:22:53.723
<i>I heard shouting up there.</i>

313
00:22:53.758 --> 00:22:55.892
Thunder.

314
00:22:55.926 --> 00:22:58.494
I know the difference
between shouting and thunder.

315
00:22:58.529 --> 00:23:01.663
Maybe it's ghosts.

316
00:23:11.574 --> 00:23:13.909
That won't help you. grandpa.

317
00:23:18.281 --> 00:23:19.948
Where you riding?

318
00:23:19.982 --> 00:23:21.983
Doesn't matter now. does it?

319
00:23:22.018 --> 00:23:24.753
No. it doesn't matter now.

320
00:23:26.456 --> 00:23:29.858
Cut his throat or he'll
tell the crows we're here.

321
00:23:35.765 --> 00:23:37.499
You understand.

322
00:23:37.534 --> 00:23:39.501
Let me stand at least.

323
00:23:40.770 --> 00:23:42.938
<i>Let me go</i>
<i>with a bit of dignity.</i>

324
00:23:47.977 --> 00:23:49.678
Make the crow kill him.

325
00:23:53.216 --> 00:23:56.619
You're one of us now.
Prove it.

326
00:24:00.825 --> 00:24:03.427
The wolves are out there.

327
00:24:06.331 --> 00:24:08.065
I can't do it by choice.

328
00:24:08.100 --> 00:24:12.137
I don't know how.
It happens in my dreams.

329
00:24:12.171 --> 00:24:14.273
You're a warg. Bran.

330
00:24:14.307 --> 00:24:16.375
It's in your blood.

331
00:24:16.409 --> 00:24:17.877
I can't.

332
00:24:17.911 --> 00:24:19.812
You just did with him.

333
00:24:19.880 --> 00:24:21.848
A wolf is nothing
compared to that.

334
00:24:29.556 --> 00:24:31.290
She looks sharp.

335
00:24:40.901 --> 00:24:42.970
Do it.

336
00:24:43.972 --> 00:24:45.439
Do it.

337
00:24:45.473 --> 00:24:48.608
I told you.
He's still one of them.

338
00:24:50.811 --> 00:24:52.378
Go on. boy.

339
00:24:55.282 --> 00:24:56.582
Go on!

340
00:25:05.358 --> 00:25:07.159
He's a crow.

341
00:25:07.193 --> 00:25:09.127
<i>He'll always be a crow.</i>

342
00:25:09.162 --> 00:25:11.529
And here's his crow wife
guarding him.

343
00:25:11.563 --> 00:25:14.766
He'll stab us in the back
first chance he gets.

344
00:25:17.703 --> 00:25:20.071
Kill him.

345
00:25:35.354 --> 00:25:37.389
- He's one of them.
- No!

346
00:25:37.423 --> 00:25:38.923
Do you hear me?

347
00:25:44.931 --> 00:25:48.233
You're not gonna die
for one of them.

348
00:25:50.036 --> 00:25:52.538
Do it.

349
00:25:52.572 --> 00:25:54.406
They'll find us if you don't.

350
00:26:24.106 --> 00:26:26.074
You were right the whole time.

351
00:26:52.066 --> 00:26:53.633
Hyah!

352
00:27:12.687 --> 00:27:15.322
<i>When you hear a
songbird's whistle. you come.</i>

353
00:27:15.356 --> 00:27:19.126
I'm a great whistler.
The greatest in the land.

354
00:27:24.004 --> 00:27:27.100
Daario Naharis.

355
00:27:54.995 --> 00:27:57.363
<i>That one was quick.</i>

356
00:28:00.133 --> 00:28:02.167
- There may be others.
- I doubt it.

357
00:28:02.202 --> 00:28:05.070
The Yunkish prefer to let their
slaves do their fighting for them.

358
00:28:50.285 --> 00:28:52.987
That's what you call
a few guards?

359
00:29:17.180 --> 00:29:19.381
Come on!
What do you got. huh?

360
00:30:33.454 --> 00:30:36.156
Lord Edmure...

361
00:30:37.826 --> 00:30:40.094
I hope I'm not
a disappointment to you.

362
00:30:48.637 --> 00:30:51.106
You're a delight
to me. my lady.

363
00:30:52.742 --> 00:30:54.410
You may now cloak the bride

364
00:30:54.444 --> 00:30:56.512
and bring her under
your protection.

365
00:31:25.576 --> 00:31:27.176
In the sight of the Seven.

366
00:31:27.211 --> 00:31:30.880
I hereby seal these two souls.

367
00:31:30.915 --> 00:31:34.517
binding them as one
for eternity.

368
00:31:34.552 --> 00:31:37.487
<i>Look upon each other</i>
<i>and say the words.</i>

369
00:31:40.057 --> 00:31:42.325
Father. Smith.

370
00:31:42.393 --> 00:31:44.727
Warrior. Mother.

371
00:31:44.762 --> 00:31:47.798
Maiden. Crone. Stranger...

372
00:31:47.832 --> 00:31:49.933
- I am hers...
- I am his...

373
00:31:49.968 --> 00:31:52.102
- <i>and she is mine...</i>
- <i>and he is mine...</i>

374
00:31:52.137 --> 00:31:56.140
<i>...from this day</i>
<i>until the end of my days.</i>

375
00:32:00.846 --> 00:32:03.715
- Is that safe?
- They're long gone.

376
00:32:09.154 --> 00:32:10.687
You were right.

377
00:32:10.755 --> 00:32:13.256
I can get inside Summer's
mind whenever I want.

378
00:32:13.323 --> 00:32:15.491
Of course you can.

379
00:32:16.793 --> 00:32:18.093
North of the Wall
there are wildlings

380
00:32:18.128 --> 00:32:21.129
who can control
all sorts of animals.

381
00:32:21.164 --> 00:32:23.498
<i>But you did a lot</i>
<i>more than that.</i>

382
00:32:25.301 --> 00:32:28.403
You got inside Hodor's mind.

383
00:32:28.437 --> 00:32:31.272
They can't do that
north of the Wall?

384
00:32:33.610 --> 00:32:35.711
No one can do that...

385
00:32:35.745 --> 00:32:36.846
<i>anywhere.</i>

386
00:32:43.520 --> 00:32:46.155
When I was looking
through Summer's eyes.

387
00:32:46.189 --> 00:32:47.856
- I saw Jon.
- Where?

388
00:32:47.891 --> 00:32:49.658
He was with the wildlings.

389
00:32:49.692 --> 00:32:51.727
They tried to kill him.
but he got away.

390
00:32:51.761 --> 00:32:53.395
<i>He'll be heading back
to Castle Black. then.</i>

391
00:32:53.430 --> 00:32:55.264
That's where we should go.

392
00:32:55.298 --> 00:32:57.666
For all we know. Castle
Black's already under attack.

393
00:32:57.701 --> 00:33:00.502
- If this many wildlings got through...
- I already told you.

394
00:33:00.570 --> 00:33:02.538
I'm not going
north of the Wall.

395
00:33:02.572 --> 00:33:05.541
Everything Jojen
told me is true.

396
00:33:07.477 --> 00:33:09.745
You saw what I did to Hodor.

397
00:33:09.779 --> 00:33:11.747
<i>I have to find</i>
<i>the three-eyed raven.</i>

398
00:33:11.781 --> 00:33:13.349
Listen to me. little lord.

399
00:33:13.383 --> 00:33:14.616
Don't worry.

400
00:33:14.650 --> 00:33:17.753
I'm not asking you
to come with me.

401
00:33:19.690 --> 00:33:21.457
It won't be safe for Rickon.

402
00:33:21.492 --> 00:33:24.561
Me?
I'm coming with you.

403
00:33:24.595 --> 00:33:27.097
No.

404
00:33:27.131 --> 00:33:29.766
You and Osha and Shaggydog
head for the Last Hearth.

405
00:33:29.801 --> 00:33:33.003
The Umbers are our bannermen.
They'll protect you.

406
00:33:33.038 --> 00:33:34.772
I'm coming with you.

407
00:33:34.806 --> 00:33:36.674
I'm your brother.

408
00:33:36.708 --> 00:33:39.010
I have to protect you.

409
00:33:40.913 --> 00:33:44.248
Right now I have
to protect you.

410
00:33:44.283 --> 00:33:47.418
Robb's at war and I'm
going beyond the Wall.

411
00:33:47.452 --> 00:33:49.821
If something happens to us.

412
00:33:49.855 --> 00:33:51.923
you're the heir to Winterfell.

413
00:33:53.959 --> 00:33:56.161
Would you know how
to find the Last Hearth?

414
00:33:56.195 --> 00:33:59.298
You southerners build your big
castles and you never move.

415
00:33:59.332 --> 00:34:00.966
You're easy to find.

416
00:34:01.034 --> 00:34:03.736
We're not southerners.

417
00:34:03.770 --> 00:34:06.839
And I don't want to leave you.

418
00:34:06.873 --> 00:34:09.675
Shh. shh.
Come here. little soldier.

419
00:34:11.144 --> 00:34:14.747
You and me. we're gonna
have some adventures.

420
00:34:14.782 --> 00:34:17.150
You don't have to do
any of this.

421
00:34:18.485 --> 00:34:19.952
Your family took me in

422
00:34:19.987 --> 00:34:22.322
and was good to me when
they had no cause to be.

423
00:34:22.356 --> 00:34:24.691
<i>Shh.</i>

424
00:34:24.725 --> 00:34:26.993
We'll be fine. you and me.

425
00:34:27.027 --> 00:34:29.262
The Umbers are great warriors.

426
00:34:29.296 --> 00:34:31.931
Even I heard
about them growing up.

427
00:34:31.966 --> 00:34:34.334
They'll teach you
how to swing a sword.

428
00:34:34.368 --> 00:34:37.904
I know how to swing a sword.

429
00:34:44.811 --> 00:34:47.580
You're leaving now? It's
the middle of the night.

430
00:34:47.614 --> 00:34:49.482
I learned to walk in darkness.

431
00:34:51.952 --> 00:34:53.653
Say your good-byes.
little man.

432
00:35:01.594 --> 00:35:03.829
Keep this one safe.

433
00:35:05.598 --> 00:35:07.665
He means the world to me.

434
00:35:28.756 --> 00:35:31.290
We've been waiting a long time.

435
00:35:33.527 --> 00:35:35.328
Haven't we?

436
00:35:36.830 --> 00:35:38.264
I don't know. you tell me.

437
00:35:38.299 --> 00:35:40.500
How long does it take
to sack a city?

438
00:35:48.742 --> 00:35:50.843
It was just as you said.

439
00:35:50.877 --> 00:35:54.279
They did not believe
until it was too late.

440
00:35:54.313 --> 00:35:56.314
Their slave soldiers

441
00:35:56.349 --> 00:35:59.818
threw down their spears
and surrendered.

442
00:36:03.922 --> 00:36:06.491
And Daario Naharis?

443
00:36:27.048 --> 00:36:29.616
The city is yours. my queen.

444
00:36:52.741 --> 00:36:54.275
They're good. aren't they?

445
00:36:54.309 --> 00:36:56.043
They ought to be
because they cost enough.

446
00:37:03.252 --> 00:37:06.454
Look at the crowd there.

447
00:37:09.891 --> 00:37:12.093
He complained
about this marriage

448
00:37:12.160 --> 00:37:14.362
the entire ride from Riverrun.

449
00:37:14.396 --> 00:37:15.897
<i>and now look at him.</i>

450
00:37:15.931 --> 00:37:17.898
<i>The gods
love to reward a fool.</i>

451
00:37:17.933 --> 00:37:20.434
- Uncle.
- What?

452
00:37:20.468 --> 00:37:23.437
He's my nephew.
I love him.

453
00:37:23.471 --> 00:37:25.473
And he's a damned fool.

454
00:37:30.845 --> 00:37:33.247
Don't you drink. Lord Bolton?

455
00:37:33.281 --> 00:37:35.583
Never do. my lady.
Dulls the senses.

456
00:37:35.617 --> 00:37:37.852
That's the point.

457
00:37:37.886 --> 00:37:39.687
Didn't you marry
one of these Frey girls?

458
00:37:39.721 --> 00:37:41.189
Aye.

459
00:37:41.223 --> 00:37:43.291
Lord Walder let me choose
any of his granddaughters

460
00:37:43.325 --> 00:37:47.428
and promised me the girl's
weight in silver as a dowry.

461
00:37:47.496 --> 00:37:49.297
So I have a fat young bride.

462
00:37:51.333 --> 00:37:53.301
I hope she makes you
very happy.

463
00:37:53.335 --> 00:37:55.136
Well. she's made me very rich.

464
00:37:55.204 --> 00:37:57.806
Pardon. my lord. my lady.

465
00:37:57.840 --> 00:38:00.308
I need to find
a tree to piss on.

466
00:38:02.378 --> 00:38:04.713
My mother's alone
with Roose Bolton.

467
00:38:04.780 --> 00:38:06.181
I should rescue her.

468
00:38:06.215 --> 00:38:08.149
Your mother is less
in need of rescue

469
00:38:08.184 --> 00:38:10.151
than any woman I've ever met.

470
00:38:10.186 --> 00:38:11.253
Be kind.

471
00:38:11.287 --> 00:38:13.288
She's finally starting
to like you.

472
00:38:14.957 --> 00:38:16.758
And I like her.

473
00:38:16.793 --> 00:38:19.995
But if she had her way.
I would be back in Volantis

474
00:38:20.029 --> 00:38:23.298
playing my harp and you
would be sitting over there

475
00:38:23.333 --> 00:38:26.335
<i>eating blackberries</i>
<i>out of Roslin Frey's hand.</i>

476
00:38:26.369 --> 00:38:28.537
Perhaps I've made
a terrible mistake.

477
00:38:31.441 --> 00:38:34.343
Striking your king
is an act of treason.

478
00:38:37.681 --> 00:38:39.449
No. don't.

479
00:38:40.384 --> 00:38:42.018
Don't insult them.

480
00:38:44.688 --> 00:38:46.689
Your Grace.

481
00:38:53.463 --> 00:38:57.366
The septon has prayed
his prayers.

482
00:38:57.400 --> 00:38:59.601
<i>some words were said.</i>

483
00:38:59.636 --> 00:39:01.436
and Lord Edmure

484
00:39:01.504 --> 00:39:04.405
has wrapped my daughter
in a cloak.

485
00:39:04.440 --> 00:39:08.877
But they are not yet
man and wife.

486
00:39:08.911 --> 00:39:11.480
A sword needs a sheath.

487
00:39:17.720 --> 00:39:21.289
And a wedding needs a bedding.

488
00:39:21.324 --> 00:39:23.191
What does my sire say?

489
00:39:23.226 --> 00:39:26.228
To bed! To bed! To bed!

490
00:39:31.534 --> 00:39:33.936
If you think the time
is right. Lord Walder.

491
00:39:33.970 --> 00:39:38.173
by all means. let us bed them.

492
00:39:44.781 --> 00:39:47.450
To bed! To bed! To bed!

493
00:39:53.457 --> 00:39:55.959
<i>Go on!</i>

494
00:40:13.645 --> 00:40:16.747
Oh!
Careful now. ladies.

495
00:40:16.781 --> 00:40:18.815
Once you set that monster free.

496
00:40:18.850 --> 00:40:21.618
there's no caging him again.

497
00:40:21.652 --> 00:40:24.954
To bed! To bed! To bed!

498
00:40:28.692 --> 00:40:30.293
Poor girl.

499
00:40:30.327 --> 00:40:33.229
Every bride suffers the same.

500
00:40:33.263 --> 00:40:35.865
I'm sure you endured
yours with grace.

501
00:40:35.899 --> 00:40:38.401
Oh. Ned forbade it.

502
00:40:38.436 --> 00:40:41.638
He said it wouldn't be right if he broke
a man's jaw on our wedding night.

503
00:40:50.115 --> 00:40:53.216
That is a very strange custom.

504
00:40:53.251 --> 00:40:55.152
I suppose it does seem strange

505
00:40:55.186 --> 00:40:56.853
from a foreigner's perspective.

506
00:40:56.888 --> 00:40:58.689
It seems normal to you?

507
00:40:58.756 --> 00:41:01.125
It's a tradition.

508
00:41:02.961 --> 00:41:05.829
Without the bedding ceremony.
there's no real proof

509
00:41:05.864 --> 00:41:08.399
the lord and lady
consummated their marriage.

510
00:41:08.433 --> 00:41:11.769
But there are other ways
of providing proof.

511
00:41:14.139 --> 00:41:15.906
Boy or girl?

512
00:41:18.277 --> 00:41:19.978
I don't know.

513
00:41:20.012 --> 00:41:23.181
But if it's a boy. I know
what we should name him.

514
00:41:23.215 --> 00:41:25.383
Oh. do you?

515
00:41:25.417 --> 00:41:28.854
It seems to me the father should
have some say in his son's naming.

516
00:41:28.921 --> 00:41:30.255
Eddard.

517
00:41:33.926 --> 00:41:35.961
Don't you want to teach
little Ned Stark

518
00:41:35.995 --> 00:41:38.430
how to ride horses?

519
00:41:38.464 --> 00:41:40.665
I do.

520
00:42:36.587 --> 00:42:38.755
<i>Go on. line 'em up!</i>

521
00:42:55.408 --> 00:42:57.810
Whoa. whoa. whoa. whoa.

522
00:43:01.081 --> 00:43:02.615
Where are you going?

523
00:43:02.650 --> 00:43:04.383
Got salt pork for the feast.

524
00:43:04.451 --> 00:43:06.618
The feast is over.

525
00:43:06.653 --> 00:43:09.054
<i>Doesn't sound
like it's over.</i>

526
00:43:09.088 --> 00:43:11.956
If I tell you
it's over. it's over.

527
00:43:11.991 --> 00:43:16.193
Turn this cart around
and get the hell out of here.

528
00:43:16.228 --> 00:43:18.195
Got pig's feet. too.

529
00:43:19.363 --> 00:43:21.464
Are you soft in the head?

530
00:43:21.499 --> 00:43:23.233
Turn this cart around.

531
00:43:35.879 --> 00:43:37.513
Your Grace.

532
00:43:43.354 --> 00:43:47.690
<i>I feel I've been remiss</i>

533
00:43:47.724 --> 00:43:49.458
in my duties.

534
00:43:49.492 --> 00:43:53.196
<i>I've given you meat</i>
<i>and wine and music.</i>

535
00:43:53.230 --> 00:43:55.898
<i>but I haven't shown you</i>

536
00:43:55.933 --> 00:43:59.001
<i>the hospitality you deserve.</i>

537
00:44:00.170 --> 00:44:01.638
<i>My king has married</i>

538
00:44:01.672 --> 00:44:05.108
<i>and I owe my new queen</i>
<i>a wedding gift.</i>

539
00:44:09.881 --> 00:44:12.383
Robb!

540
00:44:59.195 --> 00:45:01.296
You ready to
head home to Winterfell. right?

541
00:45:04.534 --> 00:45:06.034
<i>Feast over yet. is it?</i>

542
00:45:06.069 --> 00:45:08.570
Aye. it's over.

543
00:45:38.901 --> 00:45:40.701
Follow him.

544
00:45:43.205 --> 00:45:45.506
<i>Aim!</i>

545
00:46:14.171 --> 00:46:16.506
It's too late.

546
00:46:57.346 --> 00:47:00.448
The King in the North arises.

547
00:47:22.105 --> 00:47:24.306
Lord Walder!

548
00:47:24.374 --> 00:47:25.974
Lord Walder. enough!

549
00:47:26.008 --> 00:47:28.443
Let it end!

550
00:47:30.046 --> 00:47:32.080
Please.

551
00:47:32.147 --> 00:47:34.249
He is my son.

552
00:47:34.316 --> 00:47:36.584
<i>My first son.</i>

553
00:47:36.619 --> 00:47:39.187
Let him go and I swear
that we will forget this.

554
00:47:39.222 --> 00:47:41.890
I swear it by
the old gods and new.

555
00:47:41.924 --> 00:47:43.425
We will take no vengeance.

556
00:47:43.460 --> 00:47:47.129
You already swore me one oath
right here in my castle.

557
00:47:47.164 --> 00:47:50.966
You swore by all the gods your
son would marry my daughter!

558
00:47:51.001 --> 00:47:54.336
<i>Take me for a
hostage. but let Robb go.</i>

559
00:47:54.371 --> 00:47:56.538
Robb. get up.

560
00:47:56.573 --> 00:47:58.307
Get up and walk out.

561
00:47:58.341 --> 00:48:00.742
Please!

562
00:48:02.412 --> 00:48:05.147
Please!

563
00:48:05.181 --> 00:48:09.018
And why would I
let him do that?

564
00:48:11.655 --> 00:48:14.390
On my honor as a Tully.

565
00:48:14.458 --> 00:48:17.193
on my honor as a Stark.

566
00:48:17.261 --> 00:48:20.096
let him go

567
00:48:20.130 --> 00:48:23.233
or I will cut
your wife's throat.

568
00:48:31.709 --> 00:48:34.310
I'll find another.

569
00:48:37.081 --> 00:48:39.549
Mother.

570
00:48:40.613 --> 00:48:42.318
The Lannisters send
their regards.

571
00:49:20.148 --> 00:49:30.906
